{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"agent_message","text":"A custom in-place residual add is bitwise identical, but local timing shows it only helps at larger tensors and slightly hurts launch-dominated small cases. I’m testing a more consequential middle ground: keep the first MIOpen convolution (and therefore its required intermediate rounding), replace the 32→3 convolution with an MFMA/Triton kernel whose epilogue adds bias and residual. This removes one library launch and the final tensor pass without reassociating across the two convolutions."}}
